From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: husky-port CI <ci@husky-port.local>
Date: Tue, 4 Nov 2026 21:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb: noop s2mpu manual-control callback

The s2mpu_notify static callback registered by pkvm_s2mpu-v9 contains a
garbage cross-module address on zuma builds, and the indirect call in
exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control() trips CFI -> boot panic at 1.4s.
Skip the callback entirely for bring-up: when unregistered the stock
code returns 0 anyway (no-op), so this preserves intended behavior for
UT (no S2MPU manual control needed at boot).

---
 soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c b/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c
index 000000000000..777777777777 100644
--- a/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c
+++ b/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c
@@ -1860,2 +1860,6 @@ int exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control(bool on)
 {
+	/* Workaround: zuma CFI boot crash (callback ptr corrupted). */
+	if (1)
+		return 0;
+
 	struct exynos_usbdrd_phy *phy_drd;
